.TH MOIRA 1 "August 2026" "moira 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moira \- Claude and Codex quota monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moira
[\fI\-\-smoke\-test\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moira
is a compact GTK4/Libadwaita application that displays Claude and Codex
quota usage, local reset times, countdowns, refresh state and weekly
exhaustion semantics.
.PP
Data is collected only from structured provider surfaces: the chained
Claude Code status\-line command and the documented Codex app\-server
read\-only rate\-limit method. Missing or invalid data is displayed as
Unavailable, Parse error or Stale \-\- never invented.
.PP
The History tab shows quota series with reset transitions and
availability states over selectable 24h/7d/30d/90d ranges and
per\-service filters, plus exact daily token statistics computed only
from official Codex account usage (Claude remains percentage\-only).
.PP
Per\-provider collection toggles and typed alert rules feed native
desktop and NTFY notification channels with deduplicated exhaustion,
recovery, reset and error events. Diagnostics are sanitized and can be
copied; history can be exported as CSV/JSON; manual update checks use
strict SemVer parsing.
.PP
The Settings view can install and remove Moira\-owned Claude Code hooks
and Hermes shell hooks for privacy\-minimal agent activity display, and
probe Moira\-owned Codex app\-server sessions. Independent Codex CLI
sessions are never observed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-smoke\-test
Start the application, construct the main window, and quit after about
half a second. Intended for packaged validation; no data is written.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/moira/config.json
Versioned configuration (schema v3; normally
.IR ~/.config/moira/config.json ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/state.json
Last readings and alert deduplication keys (normally
.IR ~/.local/state/moira/state.json ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/history.sqlite3
Versioned SQLite History database (schema v4).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/activity.json
Privacy\-minimal agent activity store (schema v2).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 after a normal run or a successful
.B \-\-smoke\-test
run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moira\-claude\-statusline (1),
.BR moira\-agent\-hook (1)
